WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
i remember  feeling  oh my god you know  how did this happen  because  a care home is a place where you expect  your loved ones to be safe  jean anderson lost her father cleo in  april 2020  he died in a care home where he caught  covet 19. the culpability as far as i'm  concerned is fairly and squarely with  the prime minister  and and his health secretary at the time  was ma hancock  it's so  disappointing um and i feel really  saddened  and i feel  angry as well  because  you know when i think that my father  could still be here today  the high court says the government acted  unlawfully when it allowed asymptomatic  or untested hospital patients to be  discharged into care homes  but both boris johnson and the former  health secretary matt hancock claimed  they were not advised about the danger  of asymptomatic transmission at the time  not true says the former shadow health  secretary i was raising the issue around  care homes right at the start of the  pandemic because everybody knows when an  infectious disease hits  that you're vulnerable in care homes are  at risk we were raising the issue of  asymptomatic transmission as experts  were  the 75-page high court judgment lists 20  occasions where the government's own  advisors and scientists raised concerns  about asymptomatic transmission  minutes from a sage meeting on the 4th  of february note asymptomatic  transmission cannot be ruled out  and transmission from mildly symptomatic  individuals is likely  a month later at a nerve tag meeting on  the 6th of march professor neil ferguson  from imperial said  the w.h.o report highlighted that  infectiousness seems to be just before  and just after symptom onset  and just a few days later  the health minister lord bethel told the  lords that large numbers of people are  infectious or infected but are  completely asymptomatic and never go  near a test kit  by the end of march 2020 there are at  least nine research articles documenting  spread before symptoms so that's very  people who never get symptoms and people  who spread before they become  symptomatic it being on tv it was in  several  of the sage minutes that matt hancock  could have seen and should have seen  jean deserves answers and she needs  accountability  now she is one step closer to learning  the truth  about her father's death  ashish joshi sky news

